     The kkiillllppgg() function sends the signal _s_i_g to the process group _p_g_r_p.
     See sigaction(2) for a list of signals.  If _p_g_r_p is 0, kkiillllppgg() sends the
     signal to the sending process's process group.

     The sending process must be able to kkiillll() at least one process in the
     receiving process group.

